title The family named printf and the population was echo
prompt The baton, and this seat's own standing ask -- a printf argument assembling one line stays unread by every meter in the written-ASCII family, and closing it needs a quote-depth walk.
rota lap 5112, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; its threshold page says a lap that sees clearly cuts once, and its dual seat is the three depths of removal, where risk chooses the depth and surrender releases what the depth removes
think the ask named printf, so the first honest move was to size the class rather than build against the name
think the crude probe read non-ASCII outside heredocs and outside comments across 3,682 tracked shell sources -- 11,030 characters, and the split decided the lap
obs 10,416 of those sit in .rish, where the spoken meter already counts them as a say line or an assert message; the .sh half is 614 and nothing reads one of them
obs within the .sh half echo carries 360 against printf's 113, so the family named the smaller half of its own gap by three to one -- this lane's 20260915.223327 lesson arriving a second time
think the structural reason is the finding: a POSIX .sh file has no say verb, so the spoken meter opens .rish alone and the whole .sh emit surface stands outside the family by construction rather than by oversight
think the surface in question is the one every launcher, scan and control in this fleet is written on
obs the walk is the instrument -- a hash inside a string does not end the line, an escaped quote does not end the string, a greater-than inside a quoted argument is prose rather than a redirect
obs where a command BEGINS turned out to carry as much as the quoting: the keyword step alone is 21 of the 509, found by running the walk over the tree and reading what it missed rather than by reasoning about shell grammar
think spoken and written are split by the line's own redirect, because an emit that becomes a file is the sibling's act under the sibling's care
obs the ceiling ratchets rather than walls, and the reason is prin_matrix.sh drawing a terminal frame out of box-drawing characters -- the rule's own named exception, which a converter reading the total would take apart
think so emit_named prints apart from emit, and only the named half is a lane's to act on
obs two mutations are what make the walk load-bearing rather than decorative -- dropping the keyword step loses every branch in the tree, and dropping the quote walk lets a hash inside a string end the line, which is precisely the reading the family had called impossible without parsing
think reds first: three of the thirteen cold reds were mine and all three closed this lap
obs built_tool_freshness named two at once -- rye 15,276 seconds behind its source, and an orphaned ryekey speaking for a binary moved out from under it, which is the card's own three-move warning met from its other door
obs stash_record named two unlanded session logs, both this seat's own, testimony of GREEN laps whose work landed and whose record never did
think one of the recovered logs named a fold shelf that landed under a peer's name for the same two rows; a log that never landed is unsent work rather than testimony, so the path was corrected before committing rather than left to refuse
obs the claim-before-build habit and the endurance run's tree digest cannot both be honored -- opening the claim moved the tree under a sailing pass, so the pass was stopped, the claim landed and pushed, and a second pass read tree_moved=no at the cost of one full run
loom guard=shell_emit_ascii files_read=3682 files_with_emit=77 spoken=464 written=45 emit=509 emit_named=412 ceiling=509 control_legs=41 control_failed=0 mutations=4
loom probe=residue total_nonascii=12954 rish_residue=10416 sh_residue=614 sh_echo=360 sh_printf=113 emit_read=509 non_emit=105
loom cold_guards=316 cold_green=301 cold_red=13 cold_gated=2 tree_moved=no cadence_slice=upstream_shape
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_emit_ascii_scan.sh the quote walk, the operand region, and the two readings split by the line's own redirect
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_emit_ascii_control.sh 41 legs on real git repositories in a throwaway pen, every refusal planted and then lifted, four mutations asserted to bite
file tools/s/shell_emit_ascii_witness.rish the control's leg tally asserted beside its verdict, so a leg written tomorrow is heard the day it lands
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_written_ascii_scan.sh its exclusion clause repointed at the sibling that now reads what it declined
file tools/s/shell_written_ascii_witness.rish its closing GREEN line named a gap that is closed, and now names the meter that closed it
file .claude/rules/ascii-first.md the sixth surface seated with its measurement, its structural reason, and what it still cannot see
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the guard rostered at tier cadence, a ratchet at 509
